@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

@cindex configuration language
@cindex .cgra files
The @file{.cgra} language is INI-flavoured: a sequence of named sections, each
holding @code{key = value} directives.  A @samp{#} begins a trailing comment;
a line whose first non-blank character is @samp{;} is a whole-line comment.
Every entity is merged @emph{by name} across all loaded files, so a later file
overrides individual fields of an entity defined earlier.  The terse reference
is @command{man cgra 5}; this chapter is the tutorial.
Syntax errors in discovered files are reported and stop loading. A failed
file, including its includes, does not apply partial overrides.

@section Section types
@cindex sections
A section header is @code{[TYPE NAME]}.  Four types exist.

@subsection @code{[device NAME]}
@cindex device profile
A connection profile.

@table @code
@item port
serial path (e.g.@: @file{/dev/ttyUSB1}) or @samp{sim:} for the emulator.
@item baud
baud rate (default 115200).
@item timeout
per-reply timeout in milliseconds.
@item board
informational board tag (@code{basys3}, @code{nexys_a7}).
@end table

@subsection @code{[mode NAME]}
@cindex mode
An array configuration.  A mode either selects a @dfn{pattern} that generates
the device's R x C PE words, or places PEs by hand.

@table @code
@item doc
one-line description (shown by @command{cgra modes}).
@item pattern
@code{diagonal} (default), @code{reduce}, @code{custom}, @code{systolic},
@code{conv}, or @code{scan}.  @xref{Dataflow}.
@item op
the ALU opcode for @code{diagonal}/@code{reduce}: @code{add sub mul mac and or
xor shl shr max min abs acc const} (and @code{nop}, @code{pass}).
@item a
@itemx b
operand sources: @code{north west self zero} or @code{const(K)} (a 16-bit
immediate).  Defaults: @code{a = north}, @code{b = west}.
@item steps
@code{rows} (the device row count), @code{auto}, or an integer in 0..255.
Zero means no steps; values outside the protocol range are rejected.
@item out
output tap: @code{diag} (the diagonal PEs) or @code{pe R,C} (a single PE).
@item reset
@code{once} (default) clears PE registers at the start of each nonempty run;
@code{each} also clears them before every subsequent input chunk.
@item pe R,C = op=@dots{} a=@dots{} b=@dots{}
for @code{pattern = custom}, place one PE (coordinates must fit the selected device).  Unlisted
PEs are @code{nop}.
@end table

@subsubsection Fields accepted by each pattern
All patterns accept @code{doc} and @code{pattern}. Additional fields are:

@table @code
@item diagonal
@code{op}, @code{a}, @code{b}, @code{steps}, @code{out=diag}, @code{reset}.
@item custom
@code{pe R,C}, @code{steps}, @code{out=diag} or @code{out=pe R,C}, @code{reset}.
Set opcodes and sources on the individual PE lines; top-level @code{op},
@code{a} and @code{b} are rejected.
@item reduce
@code{op}, @code{a}, @code{b}, @code{steps}, and optionally @code{reset=once}.
Output is always PE(0,0); an explicit @code{out} or @code{reset=each} is rejected.
@item systolic, conv, scan
No additional fields. These entries describe dedicated engines; their
commands (@command{matvec}, @command{conv}, @command{scan}) choose parameters
from command-line arguments, independently of mode definitions.
@end table

Fields inapplicable to the selected pattern cause compilation to fail before
configuration or execution. This includes inherited fields: changing
@code{pattern} does not remove earlier definitions. Clear an ordinary field
with an empty assignment (for example @code{op =}); use a new mode name when
an inherited custom PE layout must be discarded.

@subsubsection Reset and state
For diagonal and custom modes, @code{reset=once} preserves register state
between chunks within one run, but starts the next nonempty run from zero.
It does not preserve an accumulator across separate @command{run} commands
or @code{mode_run} calls. An empty diagonal/custom input configures the mesh
without resetting or stepping it. Reductions reset once per run (including
an empty input, whose result is zero) and retain their accumulator throughout.

These rules apply to protocol v2 and v3. A v3 stateless diagonal may also
reset between chunks when its step count fully settles all diagonal results;
this permits NACK retries without changing the output. With fewer than
@code{min(rows,cols)} steps, routing registers can carry data between chunks,
so @code{once} and @code{each} can produce different outputs even for an
ordinary arithmetic opcode.

@subsection @code{[pipeline NAME]}
@cindex pipeline
A chain of modes; the host feeds each stage's output into the next.

@table @code
@item doc
description.
@item stage = MODE [imm=K]
one stage.  Repeat for each stage; @code{imm=K} sets that stage's immediate.
The first stage may be binary (consume @var{a} and @var{b}); later stages are
unary.
All stages and their immediate overrides are checked before configuration or
execution. A later stage that requires the west input vector is rejected.
@end table

Input vector A always feeds north and vector B west, independently of the
positions of the ALU operands. Thus @code{a=const(0), b=north, op=sub} negates A.
Each PE has one shared immediate. Two different constants on one PE are
rejected; @option{--imm} replaces both constant operands. Immediate literals
must be in -32768..65535 (signed values or unsigned 16-bit patterns).

@subsection @code{[io NAME]}
@cindex io profile
A data-binding profile for output.

@table @code
@item format
@code{dec}, @code{hex}, @code{bin} or @code{json}.
@item width
datapath width; must be 16 if supplied.
@item sep
@code{ws}, @code{comma} or @code{newline}.
@end table

@section Includes and variables
@cindex include
@cindex set
@cindex variables
A file may pull in another with @code{include "other.cgra"}.  The include is
searched, in order: relative to the including file, each @env{CGRA_PATH} entry,
the user config dir and its @file{stdlib/}, then the installed standard library
and @file{/etc/cgra}. The installed path is @file{PREFIX/share/cgra/stdlib}
by default (normally @file{/usr/local/share/cgra/stdlib}); @code{pkgdatadir}
can override its parent at build/install time. @code{DESTDIR} is a staging
directory and is not part of the runtime path. Installed includes work
without first running @command{init}.

@code{set NAME = value} defines a variable; @code{$NAME} and @code{$@{NAME@}}
expand it in any later value. Variables must be defined before use;
malformed references and undefined names are errors. @code{$$} emits a literal
dollar sign. Names use letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter
or underscore. For example:

@example
set GAIN = 7
[mode amplify]
pattern = diagonal
op      = mul
a       = north
b       = const($GAIN)
@end example

@section Discovery and precedence
@cindex discovery
@cindex precedence
Configuration is loaded from several roots, lowest to highest precedence:

@enumerate
@item the built-in defaults (compiled in);
@item @file{/etc/cgra};
@item the user directory (@env{XDG_CONFIG_HOME}@file{/cgra} or
      @file{~/.config/cgra});
@item each @env{CGRA_PATH} directory (colon-separated, like @env{PATH});
@item project-local: @env{CGRA_CONFIG} if set, else @file{./.cgra/};
@item the @option{-c} file (highest).
@end enumerate

@cindex conf.d
Within each directory, @file{config.cgra} loads first, then the remaining
@file{*.cgra} alphabetically, then a @file{conf.d/} drop-in directory
alphabetically.  So @file{conf.d/99_overrides.cgra} beats
@file{conf.d/01_base.cgra} by name---the Nginx/systemd convention.
@command{cgra config} prints the resolved paths.

@section Validation limits
Numeric tokens must be complete decimal, hexadecimal or octal integers.
Baud is positive; timeout is 0..INT_MAX milliseconds (zero polls immediately).
A new device profile defaults to 115200 baud and a 2000 ms reply timeout.
Invalid output formats, separators, coordinates and trailing section tokens
are rejected. Partial overrides remain valid; mode semantics are checked by
@command{check} and before execution at the selected geometry.

Names are at most 47 bytes, small fields 31 bytes, values and stored file
paths 191 bytes. Variable, stage, PE and loaded-file capacity limits are
checked. Oversized text is rejected instead of truncated; @env{CGRA_PATH}
is processed as a complete list. Embedded NUL bytes are rejected in config
files and vector inputs. A failed file, including its includes, leaves the
configuration unchanged.
